From: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Subject: [PATCH] soc: qcom: smp2p: enable the wakeup when DT has wakeup-source

The SMP2P interrupt is a wake IRQ, but its wakeup is disabled until user
space enables it. A remote processor which crashes while the system is
suspended signals it through SMP2P, so the crash is only handled at the
next resume.

On a Galaxy Z Flip3 (SM8350), the modem asserted while the phone was
suspended. The fatal error was only handled when the power key was
pressed, and the phone had no working modem until then.

The downstream kernel arms the SMP2P interrupt for wakeup on every edge
at probe. Keep the default here, but enable the wakeup when the node has
"wakeup-source", so that a board with a modem has it from boot.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
Built with W=1 and dtbs_check; not tested on the device yet.

diff --git a/drivers/soc/qcom/smp2p.c b/drivers/soc/qcom/smp2p.c
index af0ceea..af4102a 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/qcom/smp2p.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/qcom/smp2p.c
@@ -733,6 +733,7 @@ static int qcom_smp2p_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	 * enable wakeup source from user space, while other devices which
 	 * do not have proper autosleep feature may want to handle it with
 	 * other wakeup events (e.g. Power button) instead waking up immediately.
+	 * A "wakeup-source" property in DT enables it from the start.
 	 */
 	device_set_wakeup_capable(&pdev->dev, true);
 
@@ -740,6 +741,9 @@ static int qcom_smp2p_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	if (ret)
 		goto set_wake_irq_fail;
 
+	if (of_property_read_bool(pdev->dev.of_node, "wakeup-source"))
+		device_wakeup_enable(&pdev->dev);
+
 	return 0;
 
 set_wake_irq_fail:
